<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_user={@current_user} wide>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
    <span class="badge badge-ghost mb-4">Free · Open source</span>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
      Retrospectives your remote team will actually enjoy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg text-base-content/70">
      Collect ideas in real time, group them on a shared board, vote on what matters, and leave with clear action items.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
      <a href={~p"/auth/google"} class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
        <.icon name="hero-arrow-right-end-on-rectangle" class="size-5" /> Sign in with Google
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-20 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3" aria-label="Features">
    <div
      :for={
        {icon, title, body} <- [
          {"hero-light-bulb", "Share ideas together",
           "Everyone adds ideas at once. See them appear live, with a gentle typing indicator."},
          {"hero-squares-2x2", "Group on a shared board",
           "Drag sticky notes on an infinite canvas. AI can pre-group related ideas for you."},
          {"hero-check-badge", "Vote and commit",
           "Blind voting surfaces what matters most. Finish with owned action items."}
        ]
      }
      class="card bg-base-200"
    >
      <div class="card-body">
        <span class="grid size-10 place-items-center rounded-lg bg-primary/15 text-primary">
          <.icon name={icon} class="size-6" />
        </span>
        <h2 class="card-title mt-2 text-base">{title}</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/70">{body}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto mt-20 max-w-3xl" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
    <h2 id="faq-heading" class="text-center text-2xl font-semibold">Questions</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-2">
      <.faq question="What's a retro?">
        <p>
          A retrospective is a regular meeting where a team looks back on its recent work, talks about what went well and what didn't, and agrees on concrete changes to try next.
        </p>
        <p>
          Read more in the <a
            href="https://scrumguides.org/scrum-guide.html#sprint-retrospective"
            class="link"
            rel="noopener"
            target="_blank"
          >Scrum Guide</a>.
        </p>
      </.faq>

      <.faq question="How much does it cost?">
        <p>Nothing. Remote Retro is free and open source.</p>
      </.faq>

      <.faq question="Who can join?">
        <p>
          Every retro is private to your team. Share its link to invite your teammates; they sign in with their Google account to join.
        </p>
      </.faq>

      <.faq question="How does a retro work?">
        <p>The facilitator guides the team through each stage:</p>
        <.stage_steps />
        <p>
          Start by agreeing to the <a
            href="https://retrospectivewiki.org/index.php?title=The_Prime_Directive"
            class="link"
            rel="noopener"
            target="_blank"
          >Prime Directive</a>, share what made you happy, sad or confused, group and name related ideas, vote on what matters most, then agree on action items with owners. The facilitator can step back a stage at any time.
        </p>
      </.faq>

      <.faq question="What features exist?">
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
          <li>
            <strong>Real-time ideas:</strong>
            everyone's ideas appear live, with a typing indicator, and authors can edit or delete their own.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Shared, draggable board:</strong>
            an infinite canvas you pan and zoom, where you drag sticky notes so they overlap to form groups and label each group in place. A list view shows the same groups for naming them and moving ideas between groups.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>AI grouping and labelling (Highbeam accounts):</strong>
            when grouping starts, AI does a first pass, putting related ideas together and naming a group when an obvious title exists. Everything it does can be changed by hand.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Blind voting:</strong>
            three votes each, with totals revealed once voting ends.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Action items by email:</strong>
            when the retro closes, every participant is emailed the action items and their owners, with a link back to the retro.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </.faq>

      <.faq question="How many people should take part?">
        <p>Ideally no more than about ten. Larger groups make it easy for people to disengage.</p>
      </.faq>

      <.faq question="How long should a retro take?">
        <p>
          Budget about an hour for a sprint retrospective. Much shorter tends to stay on the surface; much longer tends to tire people out.
        </p>
      </.faq>

      <.faq question="Our team is in one room. Should we use it?">
        <p>
          It works well on a shared screen for ideas, grouping and voting. During discussion and action items, put laptops away and talk face to face.
        </p>
      </.faq>

      <.faq question="How is my data handled?">
        <p>See the <a href={~p"/privacy"} class="link">privacy policy</a>.</p>
      </.faq>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layouts.app>
